    "summary": "The colour front moves south: peak in each area, plus or minus 7 days.",
    "details": "Autumn colour starts in the north and the mountains and moves south. In Japan it is momiji (紅葉); in China hongye (红叶, traditional 紅葉), literally red leaf; in Korea danpung (단풍), also hong'yeop (홍엽), while the maple tree itself is danpungnamu (단풍나무). Dates are rough typical peaks from general knowledge, not a forecast; they shift by a week or two each year, and the area table is meant to be corrected. Altitude is not modelled, so mountain areas peak earlier than shown. China is a very rough starter.",
